### Method 1: Iterative Loop (The most fundamental approach)

This is the most straightforward and fundamental way to calculate the length. It iterates through the string character by character until it encounters the null terminator (`\0`).

```c
#include <stddef.h> // For size_t (good practice for lengths)

/**
 * @brief Calculates the length of a null-terminated string without using strlen.
 * 
 * @param str The string to measure.
 * @return size_t The length of the string (number of characters before the null terminator).
 */
size_t my_strlen(const char *str) {
    if (str == NULL) {
        return 0; // Handle null pointer input gracefully
    }

    size_t length = 0;
    // Loop until the current character points to the null terminator ('\0')
    while (str[length] != '\0') {
        length++;
    }
    return length;
}

